   "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=z^3+z^2+pz+q\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>The equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=0\"></span> has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3\"></span><br>When plotted on an Argand diagram, the points representing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3\"></span> form the vertices of a triangle of area 35</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1=3\"></span>, find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></p>",
