   "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=z^4+az^3+bz^2+cz+d\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>The equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=0\"></span> has complex roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_4\"></span><br>When plotted on an Argand diagram, the points representing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_4\"></span> form the vertices of a square, with one vertex in each quadrant.<br>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1=2+3\\mathrm i\"></span>, determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
